  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNESCO/Keizo Obuchi Research Fellowships Programme Phase VII (UNESCO/J</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since 2001 the Government of Japan committed to cooperate with UNESCO by offering 20 fellowships per year to young researchers from developing countries especially LDCs countries in the fields of Environment, Intercultural Dialogue, Information and Communication Technologies and Peaceful Conflict Resolution
Until 2015, 280 fellows from 99 countries benefited from this programme
For Cycles 2018 and 2019, two main activities of the proposed project :
1) offer 10 fellowships in 2018 and another 10 in 2019 in the above-mentioned field of studies to candidates from 140 invited Member States and 
2) update the web page to give importance and visibility in the results.</narrative>
  </description>
